      <section class="bg-[#002040] py-16">
        <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4">
          <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold mb-6" data-aos="fade-up">What the PickMyTrade Topstep trade copier does</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 mb-4" data-aos="fade-up">PickMyTrade is a trade copier and automation tool for Topstep. It takes one signal, either an alert from your TradingView strategy or a trade you place by hand on a master account, and places the same trade across one or many of your Topstep accounts at the same time. Entries, exits, stop-loss and take-profit prices stay identical on every account, and you can size each account differently with a per-account multiplier.</p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 mb-4" data-aos="fade-up">The model is simple: one master, many followers. You choose a master (source) account, connect the other accounts you own, and PickMyTrade mirrors every master trade out to the followers. There is no code to write, no plugin to install, and no VPS to run, because the whole flow lives in the cloud and works 24/7 whether your computer is on or off.</p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 mb-10" data-aos="fade-up">This works with Topstep accounts on the current TopstepX platform (which runs on ProjectX) and, where you still have them, with older Rithmic-era or Tradovate-linked Topstep accounts.</p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4 text-orange-300" data-aos="fade-up">Topstep vs TopstepX: which platform are you on?</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-300 mb-4" data-aos="fade-up">Topstep is the prop firm. TopstepX is its trading platform, built on the ProjectX infrastructure. As of mid-2025, Topstep moved new accounts onto TopstepX (ProjectX) and stepped back from the older Tradovate and other legacy connections for new sign-ups. For automation this matters, because the way PickMyTrade connects depends on which platform your account uses.</p>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-gray-300 space-y-2 mb-4" data-aos="fade-up">
            <li>New Topstep accounts generally live on TopstepX and connect to PickMyTrade with a ProjectX API key.</li>
            <li>Older Topstep accounts that you still hold on a Rithmic or Tradovate connection connect through those broker paths instead, where applicable.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-gray-300 mb-10" data-aos="fade-up">If you are not sure which you have, check whether you log in and trade through the TopstepX platform. If you do, use the API-key path below. See our <a href={localizedPath(locale, 'broker/tradingview-to-topstepx')} class="text-orange-400 hover:text-orange-300 font-semibold">TopstepX connection guide</a> for the full walkthrough, our <a href={localizedPath(locale, 'broker/tradingview-to-projectx')} class="text-orange-400 hover:text-orange-300 font-semibold">ProjectX connection guide</a> for API-key details, and our <a href={localizedPath(locale, 'broker/tradingview-to-rithmic')} class="text-orange-400 hover:text-orange-300 font-semibold">Rithmic connection guide</a> for legacy Rithmic-era accounts.</p>

          <div class="bg-[#001429] border border-blue-500/30 rounded-xl p-6" data-aos="fade-up">
            <p class="text-gray-300"><strong class="text-white">Which page applies to you?</strong> If your Topstep account is on TopstepX (ProjectX), you are in the right place; follow the API-key setup below. If you still trade a Topstep account through a Tradovate connection, use our <a href="https://pickmytrade.trade/copier/tradovate-to-topstep-copier/" class="text-orange-400 hover:text-orange-300 font-semibold">Tradovate-to-Topstep copier guide</a> instead. Both copy one master account to many followers with the same PickMyTrade subscription.</p>
