          <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold mb-6" data-aos="fade-up">Connecting your Topstep account</h2>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-2 text-orange-300" data-aos="fade-up">Connecting via the TopstepX (ProjectX) API key</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-300 mb-6" data-aos="fade-up">In TopstepX, open Settings, then the API tab, and use the ProjectX Linking option to create or sign in to a ProjectX Dashboard account and subscribe to ProjectX API access. Back in TopstepX Settings, open the API tab again and click Add API Key to generate your key. Copy that key into PickMyTrade when you add your Topstep (TopstepX) account. TopstepX API access is a separate ProjectX subscription, billed by ProjectX rather than by PickMyTrade, so check the current price and terms in your TopstepX settings before you subscribe. For a full walkthrough of the underlying connection, see our <a href={localizedPath(locale, 'broker/tradingview-to-projectx')} class="text-orange-400 hover:text-orange-300 font-semibold">ProjectX integration guide</a>.</p>

          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-2 text-orange-300" data-aos="fade-up">Connecting a Tradovate-linked or Rithmic-era Topstep account</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-300 mb-10" data-aos="fade-up">If you still hold an older Topstep account on a Tradovate connection, you connect it to PickMyTrade the same way you connect any Tradovate account, by authorizing through Tradovate's secure login; there is no API key to generate on this path. Rithmic-era Topstep accounts follow our <a href={localizedPath(locale, 'broker/tradingview-to-rithmic')} class="text-orange-400 hover:text-orange-300 font-semibold">Rithmic connection path</a>. If you are opening a new Topstep account today, expect the TopstepX (ProjectX) API-key path above.</p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold mb-6" data-aos="fade-up">Step-by-step setup</h2>
          <ol class="list-decimal list-inside text-gray-300 space-y-3" data-aos="fade-up">
            <li><strong class="text-white">Create a PickMyTrade account.</strong> Sign up and start the 7-day free trial (no credit card required).</li>
