          <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold mb-6" data-aos="fade-up">Multi-account copy trading across Topstep Combine accounts</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 mb-4" data-aos="fade-up">Running several Trading Combine or funded accounts is the main reason traders reach for a Topstep trade copier. PickMyTrade copies one master signal to every connected account at once, so you are not clicking through account after account and missing fills while you switch.</p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 mb-10" data-aos="fade-up"><strong class="text-white">Per-account sizing:</strong> every account gets its own quantity multiplier. Client position equals master position times the multiplier, and decimal multipliers like 0.5, 1.5 and 2.5 are supported, with the final quantity rounding to a whole number. That lets you run a smaller Combine at 0.5x, a mid-size account at 1x and a larger one at 2x from the same signal, while each account stays inside its own contract limit. Topstep sets its own limits on how many accounts you can hold and how they can be traded together, and Topstep's scaling plan caps the maximum contracts you can trade at a given account balance, so confirm your current account limits and copy rules with Topstep before you scale up.</p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold mb-6" data-aos="fade-up">Topstep trade copier rules and compliance</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 mb-4" data-aos="fade-up">A copier does not change the rules on your Topstep accounts, and it will not keep you compliant for you. Because every copied account trades the same signal, a setup that is compliant on the master is compliant on the copies, but you still have to keep your strategy inside Topstep's limits. The points below reflect Topstep's published rules as of 2026. Rules change, so confirm the current policy in your Topstep or TopstepX dashboard before you rely on any of them.</p>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-gray-300 space-y-2 mb-4" data-aos="fade-up">
            <li><strong class="text-white">Consistency target:</strong> Topstep asks that no single trading day makes up too large a share of your total profit before a payout. A copier does not break this, because the same trades run on every account.</li>
            <li><strong class="text-white">Maximum position size / scaling plan:</strong> Topstep caps how many contracts you can trade based on your account balance and stage. Set your master size and per-account multipliers so no follower account exceeds its own contract cap.</li>
            <li><strong class="text-white">Daily loss limit:</strong> Topstep enforces a Maximum Loss Limit (a trailing drawdown) on each account. Since the copier mirrors your master exactly, a losing run hits every account at once, so size conservatively.</li>
            <li><strong class="text-white">Lead / master account:</strong> designate one account as the master (source). TopstepX's own built-in copy feature calls the source account the Lead account. Only copy between accounts you personally own.</li>
            <li><strong class="text-white">What the copier will and will not do:</strong> it will place the same trade on every connected account with identical stop-loss and take-profit prices, sized by each multiplier, and it will let you stop copying instantly. It will not police Topstep's rules for you, cancel a trade that would breach a limit, or manage anyone else's account.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-gray-300" data-aos="fade-up">PickMyTrade connects to accounts on ProjectX (which powers TopstepX), Rithmic, and Tradovate, which many prop firms including Topstep run on. Copy trading and automation rules vary by prop firm and change over time, so always confirm Topstep's current policy before you go live.</p>
